      "statement": "For real terms \\(a_n\\), define the partial sums \\(s_m=\\sum_{n=1}^{m}a_n\\). The series \\(\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}a_n\\) converges to \\(s\\in\\mathbb R\\) when \\(s_m\\to s\\); otherwise it diverges.",
      "idea": "A series convergence question is a sequence convergence question about its partial sums.",
      "proof": null,
      "negation": "The series diverges if \\[\\forall s\\in\\mathbb R,\\ \\exists\\varepsilon_0>0,\\ \\forall N\\in\\mathbb N,\\ \\exists m\\ge N:\\quad |s_m-s|\\ge\\varepsilon_0.\\]"
