      "source": "lecture13-cluster-sequences",
      "statement": "The point \\(c\\in\\mathbb R\\) is a cluster point of \\(S\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\) if and only if there is a sequence \\(x_n\\in S\\setminus\\{c\\}\\) such that \\(x_n\\to c\\).",
      "idea": "Choose \\(x_n\\) within \\(1/n\\) of \\(c\\). Conversely, a sufficiently late term supplies a witness in each punctured neighborhood.",
