      "source": "lecture14-one-sided",
      "statement": "Let \\(f:S\\to\\mathbb R\\). The left limit \\(\\lim\\limits_{x\\to c^-}f(x)=L\\) requires \\(c\\) to be a cluster point of \\(S\\cap(-\\infty,c)\\) and means that, for every \\(\\varepsilon>0\\), there is \\(\\delta>0\\) such that \\(x\\in S\\) and \\(c-\\delta&lt;x&lt;c\\) imply \\(|f(x)-L|&lt;\\varepsilon\\). The right limit \\(\\lim\\limits_{x\\to c^+}f(x)=L\\) requires \\(c\\) to be a cluster point of \\(S\\cap(c,\\infty)\\) and uses \\(c&lt;x&lt;c+\\delta\\) instead.",
