      "source": "lecture14-continuity-definition",
      "statement": "Let \\(f:S\\to\\mathbb R\\) and \\(c\\in S\\). The function \\(f\\) is continuous at \\(c\\) if, for every \\(\\varepsilon>0\\), there is \\(\\delta>0\\) such that \\(x\\in S\\) and \\(|x-c|&lt;\\delta\\) imply \\(|f(x)-f(c)|&lt;\\varepsilon\\). It is continuous on \\(S\\) if it is continuous at every point of \\(S\\).",
